-- AFTER 30 WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN closes before it opens: both edges count
-- from the join, and 5 < 30 (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.2.2). With both
-- offsets literals the checker refuses it; the bare form, AFTER 30 WITHIN 5,
-- re-anchors and is [join+30, join+35] — never empty.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Buyer
    Seller

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay
    Deliver

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
bad MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST Deliver WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY Buyer MUST Pay AFTER 30 WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN)
